2026-06-05 16:45:11.908 | DEBUG  | logging:callHandlers:1737 | Submitting callback functools.partial(<built-in method run of _contextvars.Context object at 0x169ba8980>, <bound method Embedder._embed_sync of <src.embedder.Embedder object at 0x136693620>>, '[REVISED SUSTAINABLE AGRICULTURE TRAINING GUIDE.pdf - TABLE OF CONTENTS]\nNURSERY ESTABLISHMENT AND MANAGEMENT ................................................................... 54 \n6.1 A plant nursery ....................................................................................................................... 54 \n6.2 Objectives of a plant nursery ................................................................................................ 55 \n6.3 Considerations in selecting a site for a plant nursery ........................................................ 55 \nThe choice of location is the first key step. The nursery site should be 1: .............................. 55 \n• \nNear a permanent and clean water source. ....................................................................... 55 \n• \nOn flat, well-drained land to avoid water stagnation. ....................................................... 55 \n• \nSlightly away from the main field to prevent the transmission of diseases. .................. 55 \n• \nIn a protected location from strong winds and animals. .................................................. 55 \n6.5 Nursery preparation and Lay out ......................................................................................... 55 \n6.6 Management ........................................................................................................................... 56 \nSeedbed and substrate preparation ....................................................................................... 57 \nThe seedbed should be raised about 15 cm above the surrounding ground to ensure good \ndrainage. The width should not exceed 1.2 m to allow for easy work from both sides \nwithout stepping on the bed. .................................................................................................. 57 \nThe substrate (the soil mix in which the seeds will germinate) must be fine, fertile, and \nwell-drained. An ideal mix is: .................................................................................................. 57 \n• \n1 part topsoil .................................................................................................................... 57 \n• \n1 part well-matured compost ......................................................................................... 57 \n• \n1 part sand (to improve drainage) ................................................................................. 57 \n6.7 Sowing and seedling management ....................................................................................... 57 \n6.7.1 Sowing .................................................................................................................................. 57 \n1. \nWater the seedbed well before sowing. ............................................................................. 57 \n2. \nMake shallow furrows (about 1 cm) spaced 10 to 15 cm apart. Sowing in rows makes \nweeding and thinning easier. ...................................................................................................... 57 \n3. \nFor very fine seeds (like cabbage), mix them with dry sand to ensure a more uniform \ndistribution. .................................................................................................................................. 57 \n4. \nSow the seeds sparsely in the furrows. .............................................................................. 57 \n5. \nGently cover the seeds with a thin layer of sieved substrate. Do not bury them too \ndeep. .............................................................................................................................................. 57 \n6. \nLightly firm the surface and water gently with a fine-rosed watering can. .................... 58 \n7. \nCover the seedbed with a thin layer of mulch (dry grass) to maintain moisture and \nprotect the seeds from the force of the water. Remove this mulch as soon as the first \nseedlings appear. .......................................................................................................................... 58 \n6.7.2 Nursery Management .......................................................................................................... 58 \na supprimé: 69\na supprimé: 69\na supprimé: 69\na supprimé: 70\na supprimé: 70\na supprimé: 70\na supprimé: 70\na supprimé: 70\na supprimé: 70\na supprimé: 70\na supprimé: 71\na supprimé: 71\na supprimé: 71\na supprimé: 72\na supprimé: 72\na supprimé: 72\na supprimé: 72\na supprimé: 72\na supprimé: 72\na supprimé: 72\na supprimé: 72\na supprimé: 72\na supprimé: 72\na supprimé: 72\na supprimé: 72\na supprimé: 72\na supprimé: 73\n7', False) with args () and kwargs {} to thread worker queue
