2026-06-05 16:47:49.369 | DEBUG  | logging:callHandlers:1737 | Submitting callback functools.partial(<built-in method run of _contextvars.Context object at 0x1697acc00>, <bound method Embedder._embed_sync of <src.embedder.Embedder object at 0x136693620>>, "[SUSTAINABLE AGRICULTURE TRAINING GUIDE.pdf - CLIMATE-SMART AGRICULTURE]\nPREFACE \nThere is a massive demand today for agricultural products grown without excessive reliance \non chemicals. A large portion of the world's population is interested in a holistic approach to \nhealth and is willing to invest in products from sustainable agricultural practices. \nHistorically, Uganda, like many nations, has practiced traditional agriculture in harmony \nwith nature. However, to meet the needs of a growing population, programs encouraged the \nuse of chemical fertilizers to increase yields, which sometimes had negative impacts on soil \nand consumer health. Today, to reverse this trend, many countries, including Uganda, are \nturning to more sustainable agricultural practices, which has led to improved organic \nexports and farmer incomes. The Ugandan government actively supports this transition \nthrough programs aimed at improving agricultural production, soil health, and the adoption \nof sustainable scientific techniques. \nThe objective of this training manual is to provide a detailed overview of the principles and \npractices of Climate-Smart Agriculture (CSA), specifically adapted to the context of the LEAD \nproject in Palabek. The ambition of this initiative is to make farmers, researchers, extension \nworkers, and all other stakeholders aware of the knowledge and practices based on the \nprinciples of self-sufficiency and environmental protection. \nWith this conviction, I congratulate the dedicated team that contributed to this compilation. \nI hope this manual will be an effective training tool for participants, trainers, and all project \npartners. I am confident that, through this publication, we can take another step towards an \nautonomous and sustainable agriculture.", False) with args () and kwargs {} to thread worker queue
