2026-06-05 16:48:13.025 | DEBUG  | logging:callHandlers:1737 | Submitting callback functools.partial(<built-in method run of _contextvars.Context object at 0x31f9c0540>, <bound method Embedder._embed_sync of <src.embedder.Embedder object at 0x136693620>>, '[SUSTAINABLE AGRICULTURE TRAINING GUIDE.docx - INTRODUCTION TO SUSTAINABLE AGRICULTURE]\nThis is a useful tool that is used when establishing contours on the farm. It is used to find places of the same height above sea level so that barriers can be made to stop the water from washing down the soil. As the name suggest, it resembles letter A.\n3.10.1 Materials for making a frame\nThe following are the materials required to make it;\n2 straight poles (about 2 meters long) about 6 ft long (length varies with height of a person to use it)\n1 other pole about1½ m about 4 ft long\n3 nails and string\nSmall stone with regular shape (size of fist)\nPiece of charcoal/pencil/pen/sharp item\n3.10.2 Making A - frame\nStep 1\nCollect 3 sticks; two of equal size and length and 1 shorter than the two\nTie or nail the two sticks together tightly at the top\nSpread the two poles at an angle of 45 degrees to make capital A shape\nTie / nail the shorter pole (1 m) long about half way the two poles. This will form a complete capital A shape\nNote: If you are just trying, make sure the ties are very tight so that they cannot move', False) with args () and kwargs {} to thread worker queue
