2026-06-05 16:48:16.282 | DEBUG  | logging:callHandlers:1737 | Submitting callback functools.partial(<built-in method run of _contextvars.Context object at 0x31f9a02c0>, <bound method Embedder._embed_sync of <src.embedder.Embedder object at 0x136693620>>, '[SUSTAINABLE AGRICULTURE TRAINING GUIDE.docx - INTRODUCTION TO SUSTAINABLE AGRICULTURE]\nStep 4\nTo get the level mark, you measure the distance between point A and B then get the midpoint (half way of point A and B) then mark it as the Level Mark. This is the most important mark on the A frame and should be made darker or use a sharp pointed tool to make it dominant\nNote: If you’re ‘A’ string touched the same point on the cross bar in both positions, then that will automatically be your Level Mark.\n3.10.3 Using an A frame to find contour lines\nA contour line is a line that marks the points that are exactly at same level. A frame helps to find the contour line so as to avoid soil and water loss.\nSteps:\nCollect a number of pegs of 30cm to act as markers\nPush one (1st) of them into the soil starting at the top of the slope\nPlace one leg of the A frame so that it touches the first peg, then rotate the 2nd leg until the string touches the level mark\nPush another 2nd peg into the soil below the leg\nMove the 1st leg so that it now touches 2nd peg\nContinue moving (rotating) the 2nd leg looking for the level point until the string strikes it\nPush a 3rd peg into the soil below the leg of the A frame\nContinue rotating the A frame and pushing the pegs into the soil wherever the string strikes the level mark\nNote: If one leg enters a hole, it will not measure well. Therefore, fill the hole with a little soil then continue with the marking.\nAfter completion the line of pegs will have sharp bends (or some will be outside the line).  It will be difficult to dig trenches with such corners and therefore before digging, try to move those few pegs into a more even line, but should not make the line straight, in order not to lose the contour\nNow the contour line is formed and all the successive farm operations like Ploughing, sowing, laying trash or stone bands, digging contours etc. should follow or be along that contour line.', False) with args () and kwargs {} to thread worker queue
