2026-06-05 16:48:16.846 | DEBUG  | logging:callHandlers:1737 | Submitting callback functools.partial(<built-in method run of _contextvars.Context object at 0x169c1a9c0>, <bound method Embedder._embed_sync of <src.embedder.Embedder object at 0x136693620>>, '[SUSTAINABLE AGRICULTURE TRAINING GUIDE.docx - INTRODUCTION TO SUSTAINABLE AGRICULTURE]\n3.10.4 Locating the distance between contours\nIt is important for a farmer to know how to locate contour positions on the farm for purpose of soil erosion control or soil and water conservation. Soil and water conservation barriers established along contours reduce the speed and distance over which water flows, thus reducing its ability to erode. The position of contours is determined as follows:\nDrive the 1st peg to the ground (at the uppermost boundary of your field) at a point on the 1st contour. \nThe position of this peg is now our reference point\nMove down backwards with your arm stretched horizontally at shoulder level until it becomes level with your reference point above.\nDrive a peg at this point. \nThis is a starting position for locating the contour.', False) with args () and kwargs {} to thread worker queue
