2026-06-05 16:52:41.894 | DEBUG  | logging:callHandlers:1737 | Submitting callback functools.partial(<built-in method run of _contextvars.Context object at 0x169b94780>, <bound method Embedder._embed_sync of <src.embedder.Embedder object at 0x136693620>>, '[REVISED SUSTAINABLE AGRICULTURE TRAINING GUIDE.pdf - SUSTAINABLE AGRICULTURE]\nFOREWORD \nFood quality and safety are fundamental pillars for the well-being of our communities. In a \ncontext where environmental challenges are increasingly present, consumer confidence and \nfarmer resilience are being tested. Intensive conventional agriculture, while productive in \nthe short term, can sometimes degrade our soils and affect the sustainability of our food \nsystems. \nFaced with these challenges, there is a growing demand for safer, higher-quality food \nproduced locally through agricultural systems that are environmentally friendly, \neconomically viable, and socially just. Climate-Smart Agriculture (CSA), which integrates \nprinciples of organic and sustainable farming, meets these requirements. It represents one \nof the best choices for farmers and consumers, ensuring food safety from farm to plate. \nThis training manual has been specifically designed for the LEAD (Local, Empowerment and \nDevelopment) project in the Palabek refugee settlement and its host communities. It aims to \nstrengthen food security, generate rural employment, reduce poverty, and conserve our \nprecious natural resources. The Ugandan government has implemented numerous programs \nto encourage sustainable agriculture, and this manual aligns with that national vision. \nBy promoting consumer health, the ecological health of our environment, and economic \ngrowth through income generation, sustainable and climate-smart agriculture is a holistic \napproach for a prosperous future. \n2', False) with args () and kwargs {} to thread worker queue
