2026-06-05 16:53:27.349 | DEBUG  | logging:callHandlers:1737 | Submitting callback functools.partial(<built-in method run of _contextvars.Context object at 0x167e46900>, <bound method Embedder._embed_sync of <src.embedder.Embedder object at 0x136693620>>, '[REVISED SUSTAINABLE AGRICULTURE TRAINING GUIDE_2026.docx - PREFACE]\nClimate-Smart Agriculture (CSA) is not a strict set of rules, but an approach to transform our agricultural systems to effectively address the challenges of climate change. It helps us tackle the specific challenges of Palabek, such as limited land availability and unpredictable rainfall.\nCSA is based on three main pillars:\nSustainably increasing agricultural productivity and incomes (food security).\nAdapting and building resilience to climate change (adaptation).\nReducing greenhouse gas emissions, where possible (mitigation).\nThis approach is flexible. It incorporates organic farming practices like composting and mulching, but also recognizes that, in certain situations, the controlled and judicious use of artificial fertilizers may be necessary to ensure crop health and economic viability, as will be demonstrated on the cash crop plots.\n Fundamental Principles of CSA in Palabek', False) with args () and kwargs {} to thread worker queue
