2026-06-05 16:54:16.882 | DEBUG  | logging:callHandlers:1737 | Submitting callback functools.partial(<built-in method run of _contextvars.Context object at 0x167e46900>, <bound method Embedder._embed_sync of <src.embedder.Embedder object at 0x136693620>>, '[REVISED SUSTAINABLE AGRICULTURE TRAINING GUIDE.docx - SUSTAINABLE AGRICULTURE]\nFOREWORD\nFood quality and safety are fundamental pillars for the well-being of our communities. In a context where environmental challenges are increasingly present, consumer confidence and farmer resilience are being tested. Intensive conventional agriculture, while productive in the short term, can sometimes degrade our soils and affect the sustainability of our food systems.\nFaced with these challenges, there is a growing demand for safer, higher-quality food produced locally through agricultural systems that are environmentally friendly, economically viable, and socially just. Climate-Smart Agriculture (CSA), which integrates principles of organic and sustainable farming, meets these requirements. It represents one of the best choices for farmers and consumers, ensuring food safety from farm to plate.\nThis training manual has been specifically designed for the LEAD (Local, Empowerment and Development) project in the Palabek refugee settlement and its host communities. It aims to strengthen food security, generate rural employment, reduce poverty, and conserve our precious natural resources. The Ugandan government has implemented numerous programs to encourage sustainable agriculture, and this manual aligns with that national vision.\nBy promoting consumer health, the ecological health of our environment, and economic growth through income generation, sustainable and climate-smart agriculture is a holistic approach for a prosperous future.\nI take this opportunity to congratulate and express my gratitude to the team that contributed to the development of this revised manual. May this training tool help build a nation that is healthy nutritionally, ecologically, and economically.', False) with args () and kwargs {} to thread worker queue
